-- Smudge is unregistered, so s 6(1) cannot bite however tagless he is.
#ASSERT NOT `the owner must ensure the cat is wearing its registration tag` `Anne and Smudge`

`the tag came off in a fight` MEANS Section6Defence WITH
    `the act or default of another person`   IS FALSE
    `an accident`                            IS TRUE
    `some other cause beyond the accused's control` IS FALSE
    `the accused took reasonable precautions` IS TRUE
    `the accused could not by the exercise of due diligence have prevented the offence` IS TRUE

`the tag came off and nothing was done` MEANS Section6Defence WITH
    `the act or default of another person`   IS FALSE
    `an accident`                            IS TRUE
    `some other cause beyond the accused's control` IS FALSE
    `the accused took reasonable precautions` IS FALSE
    `the accused could not by the exercise of due diligence have prevented the offence` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the section 6(3) defence is established` `the tag came off in a fight`
-- Paragraph (a) alone is not the defence: (b) is a separate conjunct.
#ASSERT NOT `the section 6(3) defence is established` `the tag came off and nothing was done`
#ASSERT `paragraph (a) of section 6(3) is made out` `the tag came off and nothing was done`

§§ `7 -- illustrations`

`cutting a tag off a stray` MEANS Section7Conduct WITH
    `the tag was worn by a cat`  IS TRUE
    `removed the tag`            IS TRUE
    `interfered with the tag`    IS FALSE
    `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS FALSE

`a vet removing a tag to treat the cat` MEANS Section7Conduct WITH
    `the tag was worn by a cat`  IS TRUE
    `removed the tag`            IS TRUE
    `interfered with the tag`    IS FALSE
    `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 7` `cutting a tag off a stray`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 7` `a vet removing a tag to treat the cat`

§§ `9 -- illustrations`

`Chloe applies for Smudge` MEANS Application WITH
    `applicant`      IS `Chloe, aged 12`
    `situation`      IS `Anne and Smudge`
    `for`            IS `the grant of registration`
    `convictions in the previous 3 years for offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS 0
    `a requirement under section 9(5) was made`      IS FALSE
    `the specified time in days`                     IS NOTHING
    `the applicant complied within the specified time` IS FALSE

`Anne applies for Mittens` MEANS Application WITH
    `applicant`      IS `Anne`
    `situation`      IS `Mittens out walking, tagged`
    `for`            IS `the renewal of registration`
    `convictions in the previous 3 years for offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS 0
    `a requirement under section 9(5) was made`      IS FALSE
    `the specified time in days`                     IS NOTHING
    `the applicant complied within the specified time` IS FALSE

-- s 9(2)(a): a child applicant is a mandatory refusal.
#ASSERT `a ground in section 9(2) applies` `Chloe applies for Smudge` FALSE FALSE
-- A compliant renewal by an adult: no ground applies, so by "if, and only if"
-- refusal is forbidden.
#ASSERT NOT `a ground in section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Mittens` FALSE FALSE

`Anne applies for Smudge` MEANS Application WITH
    `applicant`      IS `Anne`
    `situation`      IS `Anne and Smudge`
    `for`            IS `the grant of registration`
    `convictions in the previous 3 years for offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS 0
    `a requirement under section 9(5) was made`      IS FALSE
    `the specified time in days`                     IS NOTHING
    `the applicant complied within the specified time` IS FALSE

-- Smudge is neither microchipped nor sterilised, and no exemption is supplied:
-- grounds (c) and (d) both apply.
#ASSERT `ground (c) of section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge` FALSE
#ASSERT `ground (d) of section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge` FALSE
-- s 9(3) and s 9(4): with the exemptions supplied, neither ground applies, and
-- the local government must not refuse on either.
#ASSERT NOT `ground (c) of section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ground (d) of section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge` TRUE

-- s 9(5): a requirement specifying longer than 21 days is outside the power.
`Anne applies, given 30 days to answer` MEANS Application WITH
    `applicant`      IS `Anne`
    `situation`      IS `Anne and Smudge`
    `for`            IS `the grant of registration`
    `convictions in the previous 3 years for offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS 0
    `a requirement under section 9(5) was made`      IS TRUE
    `the specified time in days`                     IS JUST 30
    `the applicant complied within the specified time` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the requirement under section 9(5) is within power` `Anne applies, given 30 days to answer`
#ASSERT `the local government may refuse to consider the application` `Anne applies, given 30 days to answer`

§ `Findings`

§§ `A-01 -- the certificate that cannot exist when the duty attaches`

-- ss 14(1) and 14(3), and ss 18(1) and 18(3), read together. The duty attaches
-- when the cat reaches 6 months. The certificate that would exempt the cat
-- "cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6 months of age". So a vet who
-- examines a five-month-old kitten and concludes that microchipping may harm it
-- cannot issue a certificate that does any work: the owner's duty attaches at
-- six months with no exemption in place.
--
-- Both halves are asserted, because the finding is the DIFFERENCE between them.

`a certificate given at five months` MEANS VetCertificate WITH
    `about`                          IS `implantation of a microchip`
    `given by a veterinarian`        IS TRUE
    `the age in months of the cat when it was given` IS 5
    `it applies in respect of the cat` IS TRUE

`a certificate given at six months` MEANS VetCertificate WITH
    `about`                          IS `implantation of a microchip`
    `given by a veterinarian`        IS TRUE
    `the age in months of the cat when it was given` IS 6
    `it applies in respect of the cat` IS TRUE

`Anne and Smudge, certified at five months` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS JUST `a certificate given at five months`
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

`Anne and Smudge, certified at six months` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS JUST `a certificate given at six months`
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

-- The same facts, except that this owner is getting the certificate re-issued
-- rather than sitting on it. Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 63 is what makes the
-- difference: the duty fixes no time, so the question is whether the owner is
-- proceeding with all convenient speed, and that is a fact about conduct.
`Anne, acting promptly, certified at five months` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS JUST `a certificate given at five months`
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS TRUE

-- The five-month certificate does no work: s 14(3) spends it.
#ASSERT NOT `the cat is exempt from microchipping` `Anne and Smudge, certified at five months`
-- But the owner is NOT thereby in breach. The duty carries no date of its own, so
-- Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 63 gives the owner all convenient speed to
-- comply, and an owner who is getting the certificate re-issued is within it.
-- This pair is the whole of FORK-2: the same facts, breach or no breach
-- depending on the reading of the duty's temporal shape.
#ASSERT `the owner contravenes section 14(1)` `Anne and Smudge, certified at five months`
#ASSERT NOT `the owner contravenes section 14(1)` `Anne, acting promptly, certified at five months`
-- The same certificate, issued a month later, exempts the cat entirely.
#ASSERT `the cat is exempt from microchipping` `Anne and Smudge, certified at six months`
#ASSERT NOT `the owner contravenes section 14(1)` `Anne and Smudge, certified at six months`

§§ `A-02 -- sterilised, but not by a veterinarian`

-- s 3(1) defines `sterilised` as "made permanently infertile by a surgical
-- procedure" and says nothing about who performs it. s 18(1) requires the owner
-- to ensure the cat is "sterilised BY A VETERINARIAN". s 9(2)(d) makes refusal
-- of registration mandatory where "the cat is not sterilised" -- the defined
-- term, not the s 18(1) formula.
--
-- So for a cat sterilised by someone who is not a veterinarian: the owner
-- breaches s 18(1), and the local government must NOT refuse registration on
-- ground (d), because the cat is `sterilised` as the Act defines it.

`Smudge, sterilised by a breeder` MEANS Cat WITH
    `name`                          IS "Smudge"
    `age in months`                 IS 8
    `microchipped`                  IS TRUE
    `sterilised`                    IS TRUE
    `sterilised by a veterinarian`  IS FALSE
    `registered`                    IS FALSE
    `wearing its registration tag`  IS FALSE
    `in a public place`             IS FALSE

`Anne and Smudge, sterilised by a breeder` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge, sterilised by a breeder`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

`Anne applies for Smudge, sterilised by a breeder` MEANS Application WITH
    `applicant`      IS `Anne`
    `situation`      IS `Anne and Smudge, sterilised by a breeder`
    `for`            IS `the grant of registration`
    `convictions in the previous 3 years for offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS 0
    `a requirement under section 9(5) was made`      IS FALSE
    `the specified time in days`                     IS NOTHING
    `the applicant complied within the specified time` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the owner contravenes section 18(1)` `Anne and Smudge, sterilised by a breeder`
#ASSERT NOT `ground (d) of section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge, sterilised by a breeder` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a ground in section 9(2) applies` `Anne applies for Smudge, sterilised by a breeder` FALSE FALSE

§§ `A-03 -- the sterilisation of an unmicrochipped cat is recorded nowhere`

-- s 20 obliges a veterinarian who sterilises a MICROCHIPPED cat to notify the
-- microchip database company within 7 days. A cat sterilised before it is ever
-- microchipped triggers no notice, and Division 2 adds no duty to record the
-- sterilisation when the cat is microchipped later -- s 15 requires the
-- implanter to give "the information prescribed", and what that includes was not
-- retrieved, so whether the gap closes depends on regulations outside this
-- encoding.

`Smudge, sterilised before microchipping` MEANS Cat WITH
    `name`                          IS "Smudge"
    `age in months`                 IS 8
    `microchipped`                  IS FALSE
    `sterilised`                    IS TRUE
    `sterilised by a veterinarian`  IS TRUE
    `registered`                    IS FALSE
    `wearing its registration tag`  IS FALSE
    `in a public place`             IS FALSE

`Anne and Smudge, sterilised before microchipping` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge, sterilised before microchipping`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the veterinarian owes the section 20 notice` `Anne and Smudge, sterilised before microchipping`
#ASSERT `the veterinarian owes the section 20 notice` `Mittens out walking, tagged`

§§ `18(2)(b) -- the breeder's exemption is two conditions`

`Ben and his breeding queen` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Ben the breeder`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Fremantle`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS TRUE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

`Ben and a pet of his own` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Ben the breeder`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Fremantle`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 240
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the cat is exempt from sterilisation` `Ben and his breeding queen`
-- An approved breeder's own pet, not kept for breeding, is not exempt.
#ASSERT NOT `the cat is exempt from sterilisation` `Ben and a pet of his own`
#ASSERT `the owner contravenes section 18(1)` `Ben and a pet of his own`

§ `The Cat Regulations 2012, wired to the Act`

-- The Act delegates two exemptions and cannot decide them; the regulations
-- decide them. Each situation below sets the Act's fact from the regulation's
-- conclusion, so the two instruments meet at the call site and nowhere else.

§§ `regulation 9 -- exemption from registration`

`a cat in the custody of Cat Haven` MEANS CustodyFacts WITH
    `in the custody of`                  IS `Cat Haven`
    `in foster care`                     IS FALSE
    `placed into that foster care by`    IS `nobody listed in regulation 9(3)`
    `total weeks the cat has been in foster care` IS 0

`a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for ten weeks` MEANS CustodyFacts WITH
    `in the custody of`                  IS `nobody listed in regulation 9(2)`
    `in foster care`                     IS TRUE
    `placed into that foster care by`    IS `a SAFE entity`
    `total weeks the cat has been in foster care` IS 10

`a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for thirteen weeks` MEANS CustodyFacts WITH
    `in the custody of`                  IS `nobody listed in regulation 9(2)`
    `in foster care`                     IS TRUE
    `placed into that foster care by`    IS `a SAFE entity`
    `total weeks the cat has been in foster care` IS 13

`a cat fostered by Cat Haven for two years` MEANS CustodyFacts WITH
    `in the custody of`                  IS `nobody listed in regulation 9(2)`
    `in foster care`                     IS TRUE
    `placed into that foster care by`    IS `Cat Haven`
    `total weeks the cat has been in foster care` IS 104

#ASSERT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat in the custody of Cat Haven`
#ASSERT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for ten weeks`
-- The 12-week proviso bites, and only on the SAFE limb.
#ASSERT NOT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for thirteen weeks`
#ASSERT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat fostered by Cat Haven for two years`

-- Wired: the same unregistered eight-month-old cat, in foster care from a SAFE
-- entity. At ten weeks the owner owes nothing; at thirteen weeks the duty in
-- s 5(1) has revived, on no change in the cat and none in the Act.
`Smudge in SAFE foster care, week ten` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 70
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration`
        IS `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for ten weeks`
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

`Smudge in SAFE foster care, week thirteen` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS `Smudge`
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS FALSE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 91
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration`
        IS `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` `a cat fostered by a SAFE entity for thirteen weeks`
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the owner must ensure the cat is registered` `Smudge in SAFE foster care, week ten`
#ASSERT `the owner contravenes section 5(1)` `Smudge in SAFE foster care, week thirteen`

§§ `regulation 10 -- exemption from wearing a tag`

`exhibited at a COAWA show` MEANS ShowFacts WITH
    `exhibited for show purposes at a cat show` IS TRUE
    `the show was held by`                      IS `the Cat Owners' Association of Western Australia Incorporated`

`exhibited at a show held by nobody in particular` MEANS ShowFacts WITH
    `exhibited for show purposes at a cat show` IS TRUE
    `the show was held by`                      IS `a host not listed in regulation 10(1)`

#ASSERT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` `exhibited at a COAWA show`
#ASSERT NOT `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` `exhibited at a show held by nobody in particular`

-- Wired: a registered cat in a public place with no tag, at a COAWA show. The
-- Act's duty in s 6(1) does not apply at all.
`Mittens at a cat show, no tag` MEANS Situation WITH
    `cat`                           IS Cat WITH
                                          `name`                          IS "Mittens"
                                          `age in months`                 IS 8
                                          `microchipped`                  IS TRUE
                                          `sterilised`                    IS TRUE
                                          `sterilised by a veterinarian`  IS TRUE
                                          `registered`                    IS TRUE
                                          `wearing its registration tag`  IS FALSE
                                          `in a public place`             IS TRUE
    `owner`                         IS `Anne`
    `local government of the district where the cat is ordinarily kept` IS `the City of Perth`
    `the cat is registered with that local government` IS TRUE
    `days the cat has been kept by the owner` IS 600
    `days the owner has been resident in the State` IS 2000
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from registration` IS FALSE
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place`
        IS `the cat is of a class prescribed as exempt from wearing a tag in a public place` `exhibited at a COAWA show`
    `of a class prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` IS FALSE
    `certificate about microchipping`   IS NOTHING
    `certificate about sterilisation`   IS NOTHING
    `owned for the purpose of breeding` IS FALSE
    `the owner has proceeded with all convenient speed` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the owner contravenes section 6(1)` `Mittens at a cat show, no tag`

§§ `regulation 12(2)(b) -- the renewal window, and FORK-1`

-- The reading taken is 11-31 October. 12 October is inside the window on either
-- reading; 11 October is inside on the reading taken and outside on the other;
-- 10 October is outside on both. The middle assertion is the one that changes if
-- the fork is resolved the other way, and it is here so that it cannot change
-- silently. Dates use the little-endian `Date day month year` constructor,
-- because `YMD` needs the `daydate` library and none is installed (H-04).
-- BUILDING A DATE. There is no date literal and no date constructor in scope,
-- because `daydate` is not installed (H-04). `TODATE` is a compiler builtin and
-- returns `MAYBE DATE`, so each date is unwrapped in a rule of its own and the
-- rule is what the directive asserts. The OTHERWISE arm is unreachable for the
-- literals used here; it is FALSE so that a mistyped literal fails the assertion
-- rather than passing quietly.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a renewal applied for on 12 October is in time` IF
    CONSIDER TODATE "2026-10-12"
    WHEN JUST d THEN `the renewal is within the period allowed by regulation 12(2)(b)` d
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a renewal applied for on 11 October is in time` IF
    CONSIDER TODATE "2026-10-11"
    WHEN JUST d THEN `the renewal is within the period allowed by regulation 12(2)(b)` d
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a renewal applied for on 10 October is in time` IF
    CONSIDER TODATE "2026-10-10"
    WHEN JUST d THEN `the renewal is within the period allowed by regulation 12(2)(b)` d
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a renewal applied for on 1 November is in time` IF
    CONSIDER TODATE "2026-11-01"
    WHEN JUST d THEN `the renewal is within the period allowed by regulation 12(2)(b)` d
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT `a renewal applied for on 12 October is in time`
#ASSERT `a renewal applied for on 11 October is in time`
#ASSERT NOT `a renewal applied for on 10 October is in time`
#ASSERT NOT `a renewal applied for on 1 November is in time`

-- reg 12(2)(a): a fixed-term registration always expires on a 31 October;
-- a life registration does not expire at all.
#ASSERT `the registration expires on a 31 October` `one year`
#ASSERT `the registration expires on a 31 October` `3 years`
#ASSERT NOT `the registration expires on a 31 October` `the life of the cat`
